<h2 id="find-replace">Find and revise longer articles</h2>
<ol><li>Choose Find &amp; replace beside the article formatting tools. Enter a literal word or phrase, up to 200 characters.</li><li>Find in defaults to Text outside protected regions. It skips recognized fenced, indented, and inline code; entire links and images including labels and destinations; reference definition paragraphs; bracketed text; bare URLs; escaped punctuation; and HTML markup. Raw script, style, pre, textarea, and code elements are skipped with their contents. Text between ordinary HTML tags can still match.</li><li>The scan is conservative, not a complete Markdown parser. It can exclude ordinary bracketed text, indented prose, adjacent URL punctuation, or the rest of the article after unclosed syntax. A phrase touching a protected region is skipped in full. Counts show eligible, protected, and partial-word occurrences. Choose Entire Markdown source deliberately to include all syntax, code, and addresses.</li><li>Use Next match or Previous match to select an exact occurrence in the article. Navigation wraps. Enter in Find text selects the next match; Shift+Enter selects the previous one.</li><li>Set Match uppercase and lowercase exactly when needed. Otherwise matching ignores case using the browser's Unicode rules; it does not apply language-specific spelling or normalization. Whole words only rejects matches beside Unicode letters, numbers, combining marks, connector punctuation (including underscores), and joiner characters. Hyphens and apostrophes separate words. This is not language-aware word segmentation. With the option off, matches are substrings. Matches do not overlap.</li><li>Enter replacement text, up to 500 characters. It is literal: punctuation and dollar signs have no special meaning. Leaving it empty deletes matching text.</li><li>Choose Replace selected match for the currently selected occurrence, or Preview replace all to inspect the scope, skipped counts, change count, final article length, and up to five changed passages. Apply replace all requires confirmation.</li><li>Review the changed article before approving an export. Protected search reduces accidental changes to recognized syntax; replacement text can still introduce Markdown. Source notes, review notes, title, and other page details are kept.</li></ol>
<p>Searching and previewing keep writing and approval unchanged. A replacement keeps the previous workspace under Revisions in this tab and clears approval. A result over 60,000 characters is rejected before replacement. If the current workspace cannot be checkpointed, the replacement is blocked. The history is still bounded, so download a private backup to keep important versions beyond this tab.</p>
<p>Editing the article, query, scope, whole-word or case option, or replacement clears an outdated bulk preview. Query and replacement settings and excerpts are temporary, excluded from backup files and article exports, and cleared when importing/restoring a workspace or clearing the writing desk. Applied article text is kept in the normal draft. This tool does not verify facts or link destinations, call AI, or upload writing.</p>
